  "text": "Anna waited decades in the temple for one look. Luke chapter two. Anna is a prophetess, daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Aser. Luke says she was of a great age, and had lived with a husband seven years from her virginity, and was a widow of about fourscore and four years. Translators split on that last phrase. It either means she was eighty four years old, or that she had been a widow for eighty four years. Either reading is a very long wait, and honest teachers say so rather than picking whichever number preaches better. What is not ambiguous is how she spent it. She departed not from the temple, but served God with fastings and prayers night and day. And then a poor couple walks in with a newborn to do what the law required, and Anna comes in that instant. She gives thanks to God, and she spake of him to all them that looked for redemption in Jerusalem. Decades of showing up, and she recognised him immediately, and she started telling everybody. Patience is not passivity.",
